{"name":"Golf Course","hex":"#5a9e4b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golf course","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The land where one plays golf, with tees, fairways, greens and flags in holes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golf_course"}],"entries":[{"title":"Golf course","blocks":[{"text":"A golf course is the grounds on which the sport of golf is played. It consists of a series of holes, each consisting of a tee box, a fairway, the rough and other hazards, and a green with a cylindrical hole in the ground, known as a \"cup\". The cup holds a flagstick, known as a \"pin\". A standard round of golf consists of 18 holes, and as such most courses contain 18 distinct holes; however, there are many 9-hole courses and some that have holes with shared fairways or greens. There are also courses with a non-standard number of holes, such as 12 or 14."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Golf_course_Golfplatz_Wittenbeck_Mecklenburg_Ostsee_Baltic_Sea_Germany.jpg/330px-Golf_course_Golfplatz_Wittenbeck_Mecklenburg_Ostsee_Baltic_Sea_Germany.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golf_course","wikidata":"Q1048525"},{"title":"Golf","blocks":[{"text":"Golf is a club-and-ball sport in which players use various clubs to hit a ball into a series of holes on a course in as few strokes as possible. The game was first played in the 15th century in Scotland, and as such, the country is often accredited as \"the home of Golf\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Golfer_swing.jpg/330px-Golfer_swing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golf","wikidata":"Q5377"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Golf_and_Country_Club_de_Bossey_and_the_A40_motorway_near_Geneve_in_France.jpg/500px-Golf_a